{
  "name": "To-do list",
  "description": "Open items sorted by due date, with a row tap that completes the item it sits on: the action's `serviceDataJSON` carries `{item.uid}` and `{item.listId}`, which the resolver substitutes per row before the action reaches the overlay. A placeholder naming a field the item does not have leaves that row's tap disabled rather than firing a service call with the placeholder text in it. The header outside the list reads `listStat count`, which resolves after the list settles, so \"3 left\" and the three rows can never disagree. A to-do item always carries `due`, empty when it is undated.",
